  "theorem_contract": {
    "rref_gauge_elimination": "For any binary generator matrix M in F_2^{k x n} of rank k, Gaussian elimination computes the unique Reduced Row Echelon Form RREF(M) in O(k^2 n) deterministic classical bit operations. For all A in GL_k(F_2), RREF(A M) == RREF(M) identically, completely eliminating the GL_k(F_2) row scrambler gauge from the state space.",
    "physical_group_reduction": "The rowspace-canonical oracle f_C(pi) = RREF(G_C P_pi) reduces the hidden subgroup problem strictly to the wreath product W_n = (S_n x S_n) wr Z_2 of order 2 (n!)^2, completely independent of the code dimension k.",
    "exact_involution_centralizer": "For every permutation equivalence phi in S_n, the hidden involution tau = (phi, phi^{-1}, 1) has centralizer in W_n of order |C_{W_n}(tau)| == 2 * n! identically.",
    "single_copy_fourier_extinction": "By character orthogonality and Cauchy-Schwarz on W_n, the total variation distance between single-copy Fourier sampling and the Plancherel distribution satisfies TV <= 1 / (2 sqrt(n!)) = 2^{-Omega(n log n)}. The single-copy mutual information collapses as I <= 1 / (2 ln 2 * n!) = 2^{-Omega(n log n)} bits across all rates k/n.",
    "multi_copy_commutant_intractability": "Multi-copy collective measurements require diagonalizing commutants of dimension (n!)^m = 2^{Omega(m n log n)}, creating an exponential quantum bottleneck that exceeds classical canonicalization algorithms."
  },
