  "summary": "Proved the Rowspace RREF Gauge Elimination & Self-Dual Code Equivalence Fourier Extinction Barrier. Demonstrated that Gaussian elimination RREF(AM) = RREF(M) eliminates the GL_k(F_2) row scrambler in O(k^2 n) classical time, reducing the hidden subgroup problem strictly to the wreath product W_n = (S_n x S_n) wr Z_2 of order 2 (n!)^2. Proved that the apparent Dinh-Moore-Russell dimension gate failure on self-dual codes (k = n/2) was purely an artifact of the redundant GL_k gauge. Over W_n, the hidden involution has centralizer order 2 * n!, forcing single-copy total variation distance to vanish as TV <= 1 / (2 sqrt(n!)) and mutual information to vanish as I <= 1 / (2 ln 2 * n!) bits. Formally registered NEG-ROWSPACE-RREF-GAUGE-ELIMINATION-FOURIER-EXTINCTION-BARRIER."
